L-VIOLATION-EXACT-LAND's pair is `base-569887a5` and `merge-ef2bd5c8`: the `feature/restaurant-modules`
tip and the commit that lands `lane/wf-violation-exact` and `lane/meals-violation-exact` on it together.
The +9 is exactly the two lanes' exactness suites and nothing else -- the discovered-test-set diff between
the two `.trx` files is 0 removed / 9 added, which is the number that matters here rather than the delta.
The base was measured twice, independently, before the merge (4629 / 0 / 12 both times, byte-identical
test sets); the `.trx` kept is the second run. Its full receipt is
`lanes/L-VIOLATION-EXACT-LAND/merge-receipt.md` rather than a `RUN.md` here, following the landing lanes.

L-RESERVATION-LIMITER-MOVE's pair is `base-bfe57c3c` and `lane-reservation-limiter-move`, and the
`1 failed` in the first is not a regression: `bfe57c3c` (`lane/composition-root-check`) landed a check
that was deliberately red, pending the one-line move `d9189fbd` makes. Their receipt is
`lanes/L-RESERVATION-LIMITER-MOVE/evidence.md` rather than a `RUN.md` here, following the lane above
them. `bfe57c3c`'s own pair — `base-8704ff63-fast-tier.trx` and `lane-composition-root-fast-tier.trx`
— are in this directory with no row; that lane's numbers are in `lanes/L-COMPOSITION-ROOT-CHECK/`.
(The `lane-reservation-limiter-move` row read `this commit` on `lane/confirm-postmerge-pin`, where that
was true; the merge that brought it here would have made it name the merge instead, so the SHA it
actually ran against is written out.)

`base-6771ba9a` and `lane-crypto-pin-byform` belong to the e-mail-confirmation lane family, all LANE
commits off `801d36a3`. `base-6771ba9a-fast-tier.trx` is the only receipt here that records a FAILURE, and it
records it deliberately: `EventsOutboxDeliveryTests.The_message_carries_the_link_and_no_other_guest_data`
asserts `DoesNotContain("250", …)` against a body carrying a random `PublicToken`, and the token drawn that
run contained `250`. Green on three immediate re-runs. Keeping the honest receipt beats re-rolling until the
number looks tidy — the flake is the finding.

`base-8704ff63-fast-tier.trx` was written twice, independently: L-COMPOSITION-ROOT-CHECK ran the base at
13:55 and L-CONFIRM-CONAT-RETIRE ran it again at 13:57 on 2026-08-02, and the two branches then carried
byte-different files at the same path. Both report the same run of the same commit — total 4410, passed
4398, failed 0, skipped 12 — so this merge keeps the first (blob `51e97fa2`) and does not keep the second
(blob `10a733ea`, still readable at `cfb3b14a:artifacts/tests/base-8704ff63-fast-tier.trx`). The two rows
above are both preserved because they measure different commits; these two measured one.

The full receipt for each run — command, environment, what was excluded and what is still unmeasured —
is the `RUN.md` in the directory named for its SHA.

`ffb29e4e` is a LANE commit, not an ancestor of any receipt above it: it ran on
`lane/growth-mail-postmark` off `349d8806`, which is why its count sits below the row before it.

`a7697121` is also a LANE commit — `lane/gr-confirmed-email`, one commit above the unmerged
`lane/gr-testsend-guard` — but unlike `ffb29e4e` it descends from the row above it, so its count is
comparable to `99855b1d` directly.

`3cf288fb` is the same lane two commits later and carries the identical count. It changes tests and
comments only, so ±0 is the expected result rather than a suspicious one — what changed is whether one
pin can fail, which a green tier cannot show. Its `RUN.md` records the mutations that can.

`771c0fc0` is on `lane/gr-confirm-stale`, branched off `48950702` (the receipt commit above `3cf288fb`),
so it descends from every row above it. Its +4 is one new test class; its base was re-measured at
`48950702` rather than inherited, and reproduced `4376 / 4364 / 12` exactly.

`0659666f` is a LANE commit too: `lane/meals-release` off `24dec838`, which is two commits ahead of
`99855b1d` on `feature/restaurant-modules`.

`2497ce9d` is a LANE commit too, on `lane/pdf-nullderef` off `lane/download-pdf-wire` (`a7b90cbd`), which
was itself unmerged when the row was written. Its row is not comparable to any row above it — when it was
written the row above it was `99855b1d`, and L-PDF-FAMILY-LAND's union has since put six other lanes'
rows between them. The base it IS comparable to is 4373 / 0 / 12, measured at `a7b90cbd` on that lane's
own worktree and recorded in its `RUN.md`.

`f18ffeda` continues that same stack, on `lane/invoice-retry-retirement` off `17198f14`. Its
count is IDENTICAL to `2497ce9d` on purpose: it adds assertions to two existing tests rather than new
tests, so an unchanged total is the expected reading. What changed is proved by mutation instead, and
the mutations are recorded in its `RUN.md`.

Both stacks landed on `feature/restaurant-modules` through L-PDF-FAMILY-LAND, whose own numbers —
baseline `4685fb01` and the merge commit — are in `lanes/L-PDF-FAMILY-LAND/merge-receipt.md` rather than
here, following the landing lanes above.

## The rule this directory keeps

A run recorded here was produced from a **clean checkout of one commit**, not from a working tree. The
run above was executed in a throwaway `git worktree` detached at the SHA, which is why the paths inside
the `.trx` read `wt-be-receipt` rather than the main checkout: a suite run in a shared worktree while
sibling lanes are editing it measures no commit at all, and that is the exact defect this directory
exists to stop.

Adding a run means: run it at a SHA, drop the `.trx` in with that SHA leading its name, add a row above,
and write the `RUN.md` beside it. Do not overwrite an existing row — a superseded run is still the
honest record of what was true that day.

The other way a number here can measure the wrong thing is `--no-build` over a stale assembly: see the
`--no-build` note in the repo's `CLAUDE.md` under **Commands → Tests** before recording any run produced
with it.

## What a green suite here is not

It is evidence that code behaves. It is not evidence that a capability exists or is reachable, and it
is never acceptance — acceptance is a person completing the journey.
